# tools/boundary/protected.manifest is a generated, sorted SHA256 index of the
# protected surface. Two branches that each touch a protected file produce
# different hash sets, and git cannot meaningfully three-way-merge a sorted hash
# list — so every such pair conflicted. That single file accounted for most of
# the conflicted pull requests in this repository.
#
# The resolution is always the same and never a judgement call: take either
# side, then regenerate. This driver takes ours and marks the path resolved;
# CI's `make verify-boundary` is the authority and fails on any drift, so a
# stale intermediate cannot reach main.
#
# Install the driver once with `make install-merge-drivers`. Without it git
# falls back to a normal conflict, which is safe — just noisier.
tools/boundary/protected.manifest merge=helm-derived
